iterations.reply:
I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need filesystem and HTTP authority that it doesn't have. There is also no WASI adapter. The HTTP request would additionally send the user's reply text to an outside service. If operations needs either one, the graph would have to grant those capabilities (for example `http-client` or a logging interface) in the node's `with` clause.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The channel stamps its own session identity and delivery status on the
        // confirmation; pass it through unchanged rather than fabricating either.
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

